course: dictionary
lesson: 15296
title: A skier and the -er ending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A skier is a person who moves over snow on skis, for sport or for fun. Skier is a noun, so it names a person. Skiers, with an s, means more than one skier.
explain: The ending -er often means a person who does something. A baker bakes, a runner runs, and a skier skis. «Mia is a good skier; she can ski down the steep slope without falling.» The word good tells you how well Mia skis.
explain: Skiers keep safe. «Every skier wore a helmet and goggles on the slope.» They also stay on marked runs, the paths that are checked and signed, so they are less likely to get lost or hurt. A cross-country skier travels across the snow instead of mainly down a hill.
fact: A skier is a person who moves over snow on skis.
fact: The -er ending often means a person who does something: a skier skis.
fact: «Skiers» is the plural, meaning more than one skier.
fact: «Downhill skier» means a person who skis down slopes, and «cross-country skier» means a person who skis across the snow.
fact: Skiers wear helmets and goggles, and they stay on marked runs.
exercise: Who is a skier? | A machine that makes snow | A shop that sells boots | A chair lift up the mountain | *A person who moves over snow on skis
exercise: «Mia is a good skier.» What is a skier? | A shop that sells skis | A type of snow | A warm winter coat | *A person who skis
exercise: Which word is the plural of skier? | *skiers | skis | skied | skiing
test: What does the ending -er tell you in skier? | Something that is very cold | *A person who does the action | A type of sport only for children | A place where snow falls
test: «The cross-country skier crossed the snowy hills all morning.» What is a cross-country skier? | A person who skis down steep slopes | A machine for moving snow | A person who sells skis | *A person who skis across the snow
exam: Which safety item do skiers often wear? | *A helmet | A sun hat at the beach | A raincoat in a warm room | A swimming cap
